1
00:00:25,926 --> 00:00:28,225
♪♪

2
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,371
♪♪

3
00:00:49,449 --> 00:00:51,509
♪♪

4
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:47,750
Well, thank you, Susan.

5
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:49,586
This is Brian Clayborn,
your entertainment editor,

6
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:51,955
coming to you live from
the new Rialto Theater,

7
00:01:51,979 --> 00:01:53,790
where Nicky Tower
is due to arrive

8
00:01:53,814 --> 00:01:56,225
virtually any second
now, for the premiere

9
00:01:56,249 --> 00:01:57,493
of his new movie, which,

10
00:01:57,517 --> 00:02:00,096
like many of his films, was
shot right here in Atlanta.

11
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,999
And, right now, I do believe

12
00:02:03,023 --> 00:02:05,201
he is coming up
here, and... yes,

13
00:02:05,225 --> 00:02:08,471
Nicky has arrived, as you
can tell from the crowd reaction.

14
00:02:10,163 --> 00:02:11,941
Hey!

15
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:13,343
Hey, Atlanta, love you!

16
00:02:13,367 --> 00:02:14,460
You're great!

17
00:02:20,173 --> 00:02:21,751
You're the best!

18
00:02:21,775 --> 00:02:24,387
We'll see if we can get a
word with him right now, Susan.

19
00:02:30,183 --> 00:02:32,195
Get down!

20
00:02:34,621 --> 00:02:36,733
Oh, my God!

21
00:02:36,757 --> 00:02:38,735
Did you see that?
Someone on a motorcycle

22
00:02:38,759 --> 00:02:40,670
just pulled up and
shot three shots

23
00:02:40,694 --> 00:02:41,804
at Nicky Tower.

24
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:43,539
Nicky Tower is down.

25
00:02:43,563 --> 00:02:44,841
Security guards

26
00:02:44,865 --> 00:02:47,310
from the theater
are attending to him.

27
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:49,667
Uh, back to you, Susan and Bill.

28
00:02:57,944 --> 00:03:01,557
Oh... No. No, no, no, no, no!

29
00:03:01,581 --> 00:03:02,992
Get over!

30
00:03:07,654 --> 00:03:09,065
Ben!

31
00:03:09,089 --> 00:03:12,568
Well, Sherman.

32
00:03:12,592 --> 00:03:14,771
How you doing?

33
00:03:14,795 --> 00:03:16,406
Good to see you, Ben.

34
00:03:16,430 --> 00:03:17,940
Boy, this is a switch.

35
00:03:17,964 --> 00:03:19,942
Usually when we
run into each other

36
00:03:19,966 --> 00:03:21,778
you're the one wearing the robe.

37
00:03:22,903 --> 00:03:25,648
I need an attorney, Ben.

38
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:29,152
Uh... actually, my son does.

39
00:03:29,176 --> 00:03:32,088
Well, why does he need a lawyer?

40
00:03:32,112 --> 00:03:34,924
They think he killed someone.

41
00:03:34,948 --> 00:03:36,426
He didn't.

42
00:03:36,450 --> 00:03:39,128
Believe me, he'd
tell me if he had,

43
00:03:39,152 --> 00:03:41,230
just to see the look on my face.

44
00:03:41,254 --> 00:03:44,801
Oh, you didn't...
didn't, uh... get along.

45
00:03:44,825 --> 00:03:46,002
That's an understatement.

46
00:03:46,026 --> 00:03:47,937
Sandra and I were
divorced when he was nine.

47
00:03:47,961 --> 00:03:50,106
I didn't see much of
him; I was very busy.

48
00:03:50,130 --> 00:03:51,808
You know how it is.

49
00:03:51,832 --> 00:03:54,544
I know I wasn't
much of a father.

50
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:56,946
This time, I'd like
to be there for him.

51
00:03:56,970 --> 00:04:00,616
Well, did, uh, did
they arrest him yet?

52
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,685
He's in the lockup downtown.

53
00:04:02,709 --> 00:04:05,474
Could you at least
talk to him, Ben?

54
00:04:06,847 --> 00:04:08,958
Oh, well, y-yeah.

55
00:04:08,982 --> 00:04:10,848
Yeah, I-I could do that.

56
00:04:12,886 --> 00:04:16,666
I guess I better...
put on some britches.

57
00:04:16,690 --> 00:04:18,534
All right, Sherman,
I'll put on...

58
00:04:18,558 --> 00:04:20,970
them britches in there.

59
00:04:20,994 --> 00:04:22,238
I'll be, uh...

60
00:04:31,204 --> 00:04:35,818
So... you're Sherman
Lockwood's son.

61
00:04:35,842 --> 00:04:37,487
That's right.

62
00:04:37,511 --> 00:04:40,310
Who are you?

63
00:04:42,849 --> 00:04:45,512
I'm a lawyer. Ben Matlock.

64
00:04:58,231 --> 00:05:00,777
Oh, man.

65
00:05:00,801 --> 00:05:04,347
My father didn't tell
you about me, did he?

66
00:05:04,371 --> 00:05:07,350
Well, that's all right.

67
00:05:07,374 --> 00:05:10,553
He's real good when it
comes to passing out judgment.

68
00:05:10,577 --> 00:05:14,014
When it comes to telling
the truth, very mediocre.

69
00:05:16,049 --> 00:05:18,027
No, he told me.

70
00:05:18,051 --> 00:05:21,988
And he wants more than anything
to make up for past mistakes.

71
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:26,869
He's asked me to represent
you, and I'm willing to try.

72
00:05:26,893 --> 00:05:28,304
Can you get me off?

73
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:29,472
I don't know.

74
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:31,274
I'm willing to try.

75
00:05:31,298 --> 00:05:32,942
No promises. I'll try.

76
00:05:32,966 --> 00:05:34,628
Yeah.

77
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:41,217
How are you at it?

78
00:05:41,241 --> 00:05:44,620
- At what?
- Telling the truth.

79
00:05:44,644 --> 00:05:46,489
Try me.

80
00:05:46,513 --> 00:05:49,759
Why are you in here?

81
00:05:49,783 --> 00:05:53,663
Somebody riding a bike
like mine killed Nicky Tower.

82
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:58,100
I used to work for him, so
the cops think it was me.

83
00:05:58,124 --> 00:06:00,218
That's it?

84
00:06:01,261 --> 00:06:04,595
Whoever did it used my gun.

85
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:07,643
Oh, you own a gun.

86
00:06:07,667 --> 00:06:09,078
Yeah, I own a gun.

87
00:06:09,102 --> 00:06:11,547
It's legal, it's registered.

88
00:06:11,571 --> 00:06:13,549
Police found it?

89
00:06:13,573 --> 00:06:17,486
Yeah, couple of blocks away
from where Nicky was killed.

90
00:06:17,510 --> 00:06:19,622
You didn't like him?

91
00:06:19,646 --> 00:06:22,525
I liked him fine
till he fired me.

92
00:06:22,549 --> 00:06:25,228
Now the cops are
trying to make a big deal

93
00:06:25,252 --> 00:06:26,762
out of this fight we had.

94
00:06:26,786 --> 00:06:27,997
Fight?

95
00:06:28,021 --> 00:06:29,899
Yeah, we had a fight.

96
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:32,468
He fired me for nothing, man.

97
00:06:32,492 --> 00:06:34,537
When?

98
00:06:34,561 --> 00:06:36,539
Day before the murder.

99
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:38,241
Mm.

100
00:06:38,265 --> 00:06:40,643
Alibi?

101
00:06:40,667 --> 00:06:42,945
I was riding my bike.

102
00:06:42,969 --> 00:06:44,347
By yourself?

103
00:06:44,371 --> 00:06:45,781
By myself!

104
00:06:45,805 --> 00:06:48,331
Is that all right by you?!

105
00:06:52,979 --> 00:06:55,291
You're in a lot of trouble,

106
00:06:55,315 --> 00:07:00,563
and if you don't realize that,
you're in even more trouble.

107
00:07:00,587 --> 00:07:02,765
Now, if you want
me to try to help you,

108
00:07:02,789 --> 00:07:04,567
take that cigarette
out of your mouth,

109
00:07:04,591 --> 00:07:09,906
put your feet down, sit up
and talk to me like a man,

110
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:12,729
and quit acting like a jackass!

111
00:07:29,516 --> 00:07:31,961
<i>Now, Ms. Williams,</i>

112
00:07:31,985 --> 00:07:34,931
you were Mr. Tower's
personal assistant for how long?

113
00:07:34,955 --> 00:07:36,299
For eight years.

114
00:07:36,323 --> 00:07:38,701
And were you in his
employ when he hired

115
00:07:38,725 --> 00:07:41,437
the defendant, Cliff
Lockwood, to be his bodyguard?

116
00:07:41,461 --> 00:07:43,339
- Yes, I was.
- How long ago was that?

117
00:07:43,363 --> 00:07:45,141
That was two months ago,

118
00:07:45,165 --> 00:07:47,243
right after Mr. Tower
arrived here in Atlanta

119
00:07:47,267 --> 00:07:49,245
to begin prepping
for his new film.

120
00:07:49,269 --> 00:07:52,815
Would you describe
for us the circumstances

121
00:07:52,839 --> 00:07:55,251
under which the
defendant was hired?

122
00:07:55,275 --> 00:07:58,541
Well, Nicky literally hired
him right off the street.

123
00:08:06,586 --> 00:08:09,198
Probably got fake tattoos!

124
00:08:09,222 --> 00:08:10,433
Hey, come on.

125
00:08:10,457 --> 00:08:13,436
Come on, just one joke.

126
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:15,104
It's my birthday.

127
00:08:15,128 --> 00:08:17,239
Listen, pal, I'm fresh
out of birthday jokes.

128
00:08:17,263 --> 00:08:18,908
Well, a-any joke, then. Come on.

129
00:08:18,932 --> 00:08:20,176
Excuse me, Mr. Tower

130
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,078
would just like to
go home, all right?

131
00:08:22,102 --> 00:08:25,281
Hey, I paid $6.50 to
see your last movie,

132
00:08:25,305 --> 00:08:26,716
and you know something?

133
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:28,384
It stank!

134
00:08:28,408 --> 00:08:31,687
You owe me, Mr. Hollywood star.

135
00:08:31,711 --> 00:08:34,557
Stay here.

136
00:08:34,581 --> 00:08:37,426
Hey, hey, hey.

137
00:08:37,450 --> 00:08:39,295
I got a joke for you.

138
00:08:39,319 --> 00:08:41,297
Why'd the turkey cross the road?

139
00:08:41,321 --> 00:08:44,400
Uh... I-I don't know.

140
00:08:44,424 --> 00:08:48,371
Because he was about to get
the stuffing knocked out of him.

141
00:08:54,334 --> 00:08:55,578
Hey.

142
00:08:55,602 --> 00:08:57,146
Thanks, pal. That was great.

143
00:08:57,170 --> 00:08:59,949
Did you ever think about
doing that for a living?

144
00:08:59,973 --> 00:09:01,417
What, tell jokes?

145
00:09:02,675 --> 00:09:04,553
I like this guy.

146
00:09:04,577 --> 00:09:06,956
Hey, how'd you like
to be my bodyguard?

147
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,958
- Nicky...
- I'm serious... if people see

148
00:09:08,982 --> 00:09:11,627
a biker, they're gonna run first
and ask questions later, right?

149
00:09:11,651 --> 00:09:13,996
- Yeah, why don't, uh...
- Well, what do you think?

150
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:15,215
Want a job?

151
00:09:16,790 --> 00:09:18,501
No.

152
00:09:18,525 --> 00:09:20,517
I sure do need one.

153
00:09:21,694 --> 00:09:23,390
Got a deal.

154
00:09:25,632 --> 00:09:27,777
<i>He hired him right on the spot</i>

155
00:09:27,801 --> 00:09:30,012
without even so much
as asking him his name.

156
00:09:30,036 --> 00:09:32,248
Nicky loved doing
off-the-wall things like that.

157
00:09:32,272 --> 00:09:35,518
Were you also present
when he fired the defendant?

158
00:09:35,542 --> 00:09:36,519
Yes.

159
00:09:36,543 --> 00:09:38,054
Would you describe that for us?

160
00:09:38,078 --> 00:09:40,056
Well, Gary Benton,
the producer of the film

161
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,657
Nicky was going
to start shooting

162
00:09:41,681 --> 00:09:43,192
here in town had arrived,

163
00:09:43,216 --> 00:09:46,662
and they were going over some
set sketches in Nicky's room.

164
00:09:46,686 --> 00:09:48,864
There aren't sets;
these are cages.

165
00:09:48,888 --> 00:09:51,634
Who the hell designed these
things anyway, Jiminy Cricket?

166
00:09:51,658 --> 00:09:53,769
Nicky! These are just sketches.

167
00:09:53,793 --> 00:09:56,906
You'll love the
sets, believe me.

168
00:09:56,930 --> 00:09:59,442
I'll tell you what I
believe... It's money again.

169
00:09:59,466 --> 00:10:00,943
It's your damn chintzy budgets.

170
00:10:00,967 --> 00:10:03,345
Why don't you just film
your stupid budget, all right?

171
00:10:03,369 --> 00:10:06,015
Put that up on the screen,
see how many people come.

172
00:10:06,039 --> 00:10:07,349
Nicky...

173
00:10:07,373 --> 00:10:09,452
- I want to talk to you, Nicky.
- Cliff!

174
00:10:09,476 --> 00:10:10,653
I just found out!

175
00:10:10,677 --> 00:10:11,987
Cliff, get the hell in here!

176
00:10:12,011 --> 00:10:13,222
You're gonna pay
for this, dirtbag!

177
00:10:13,246 --> 00:10:14,824
Look, I don't know
what your problem is,

178
00:10:14,848 --> 00:10:16,125
Miller, but you're this close

179
00:10:16,149 --> 00:10:17,583
to being laid off, permanently!

180
00:10:21,354 --> 00:10:23,687
Later, Nicky.

181
00:10:25,525 --> 00:10:26,669
That guy's nuts!

182
00:10:26,693 --> 00:10:27,803
Cliff!

183
00:10:27,827 --> 00:10:30,005
Where is that slob?

184
00:10:30,029 --> 00:10:32,575
Man, what's
happening? You call me?

185
00:10:32,599 --> 00:10:34,477
Only about a hundred
times, you idiot.

186
00:10:34,501 --> 00:10:36,112
- Where have you been?
- You sent me out

187
00:10:36,136 --> 00:10:37,346
for hamburgers, remember?

188
00:10:37,370 --> 00:10:39,281
That was hours ago!

189
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:41,250
There was a line.

190
00:10:41,274 --> 00:10:43,018
You like waiting in line?

191
00:10:43,042 --> 00:10:45,454
Why don't you try the line
at the unemployment office?

192
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:47,310
You're fired, bozo!

193
00:10:48,715 --> 00:10:53,142
What goes around
comes around... bozo.

194
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:02,922
You happy?

195
00:11:04,397 --> 00:11:06,976
How many times
prior to that incident

196
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,578
did Mr. Tower
express anger toward

197
00:11:09,602 --> 00:11:12,047
or dissatisfaction
with my client?

198
00:11:12,071 --> 00:11:15,918
- Well... uh, there...
- 12 times,

199
00:11:15,942 --> 00:11:17,887
six times or none?

200
00:11:17,911 --> 00:11:20,556
None that I'm aware of.

201
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:23,592
And during this
one isolated incident

202
00:11:23,616 --> 00:11:26,262
that you described,
did my client

203
00:11:26,286 --> 00:11:28,397
ever actually
threaten Mr. Tower?

204
00:11:28,421 --> 00:11:31,787
Well... Did he?

205
00:11:33,593 --> 00:11:36,372
Not in so many words, no.

206
00:11:36,396 --> 00:11:38,228
Thank you.

207
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:44,246
So, Mr. Bonzer,

208
00:11:44,270 --> 00:11:47,449
how many years have you
been selling motorcycles?

209
00:11:47,473 --> 00:11:49,919
Opened my shop in 19-and-54.

210
00:11:49,943 --> 00:11:53,022
Did you ever sell a
motorcycle to Mr. Lockwood?

211
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:54,757
Over the years,
I've sold him several.

212
00:11:54,781 --> 00:11:58,994
What was the make and model
of the last bike you sold him?

213
00:11:59,018 --> 00:12:01,920
Claymore 1200 Hyperglide.

214
00:12:04,290 --> 00:12:05,801
Was it like this one?

215
00:12:05,825 --> 00:12:08,304
Exactly like that one.

216
00:12:08,328 --> 00:12:09,872
Are you sure about that?

217
00:12:09,896 --> 00:12:12,841
The motorcycle he was
riding was identical to that one

218
00:12:12,865 --> 00:12:15,878
in make and color, I'm positive.

219
00:12:15,902 --> 00:12:18,747
How far from the Georgia
state border was Mr. Lockwood

220
00:12:18,771 --> 00:12:19,915
when you pulled him over?

221
00:12:19,939 --> 00:12:21,550
Less than ten miles.

222
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,719
Did he happen to mention
where he was going?

223
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:25,354
Said he was going cross-country.

224
00:12:25,378 --> 00:12:28,457
Did he say he was on the
way <i>out</i> of the state of Georgia?

225
00:12:28,481 --> 00:12:30,759
That's what he told
me; yes, ma'am.

226
00:12:30,783 --> 00:12:31,794
Thank you.

227
00:12:31,818 --> 00:12:33,462
No further questions.

228
00:12:33,486 --> 00:12:35,397
Mr. Matlock, cross-examine?

229
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:38,968
Yes, sir. When you arrested
my client and told him

230
00:12:38,992 --> 00:12:42,371
that, uh, Nicky Tower
had been murdered,

231
00:12:42,395 --> 00:12:43,939
uh, how'd he react, surprised?

232
00:12:43,963 --> 00:12:45,608
He seemed surprised, yes, sir.

233
00:12:45,632 --> 00:12:46,675
How'd he act?

234
00:12:46,699 --> 00:12:47,743
He didn't like it.

235
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:49,545
He, uh, was very agitated.

236
00:12:49,569 --> 00:12:51,347
He used a lot of profanity.

237
00:12:51,371 --> 00:12:54,416
Yeah. Well, when you
put the handcuffs on him,

238
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,684
how'd he react?

239
00:12:55,708 --> 00:12:59,755
Well, he tried to resist,
but I had a hold on him.

240
00:12:59,779 --> 00:13:03,492
Uh-huh. Did, did he
try to fight or run away?

241
00:13:03,516 --> 00:13:05,494
Oh, I had a hold on him.

242
00:13:05,518 --> 00:13:08,030
Just answer the question.
Did he try to fight or run away?

243
00:13:08,054 --> 00:13:10,899
No, sir, he didn't do that.

244
00:13:10,923 --> 00:13:13,051
Thank you.

245
00:13:14,827 --> 00:13:17,239
The defendant will please rise.

246
00:13:17,263 --> 00:13:21,110
Mr. Lockwood, I find that
sufficient evidence exists

247
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:22,444
to bind you over for trial

248
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:24,146
for the murder of
Nicholas Tower.

249
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:27,683
This matter will be set
for trial in Department 111

250
00:13:27,707 --> 00:13:31,620
of the Superior Court
on the 11th of February.

251
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:34,375
This court is now in recess.

252
00:13:55,802 --> 00:13:58,135
You got a light, hotshot?

253
00:14:08,314 --> 00:14:09,792
Excuse me.

254
00:14:13,052 --> 00:14:15,364
Now let me get this straight.

255
00:14:15,388 --> 00:14:18,000
You say after your
argument with Nicky Tower,

256
00:14:18,024 --> 00:14:20,569
you jumped on your bike
and you just started riding?

257
00:14:20,593 --> 00:14:22,271
That's right.

258
00:14:22,295 --> 00:14:24,373
That means you must
have been on the road

259
00:14:24,397 --> 00:14:25,808
for close to 36 hours,

260
00:14:25,832 --> 00:14:28,243
so somebody, somewhere,
had to have seen you...

261
00:14:28,267 --> 00:14:30,612
Hopefully, at the
time of the murder.

262
00:14:30,636 --> 00:14:32,247
What about waitresses?

263
00:14:32,271 --> 00:14:33,615
No.

264
00:14:33,639 --> 00:14:35,184
Motel clerks?

265
00:14:35,208 --> 00:14:39,621
I ate out of vending machines
and I slept in the woods.

266
00:14:39,645 --> 00:14:42,291
- Here.
- Great.

267
00:14:42,315 --> 00:14:44,226
That stuntman Steve Miller,

268
00:14:44,250 --> 00:14:46,729
why was he so mad
at Nicky that day?

269
00:14:46,753 --> 00:14:49,932
No idea.

270
00:14:49,956 --> 00:14:52,568
They get along?

271
00:14:52,592 --> 00:14:53,769
Yeah, Steve supervised

272
00:14:53,793 --> 00:14:55,804
the stunts on Nicky's
last three movies.

273
00:14:55,828 --> 00:14:59,475
What about, what about
that, uh, producer, uh,

274
00:14:59,499 --> 00:15:02,911
see what it says...
Yeah. Gary Benton.

275
00:15:02,935 --> 00:15:05,247
They argued all the time.

276
00:15:05,271 --> 00:15:06,448
About what?

277
00:15:06,472 --> 00:15:07,950
I don't know, man.

278
00:15:07,974 --> 00:15:09,385
Production stuff, I guess.

279
00:15:09,409 --> 00:15:10,919
I was always in the other room.

280
00:15:10,943 --> 00:15:11,920
I couldn't hear.

281
00:15:11,944 --> 00:15:13,389
We're going to work.

282
00:15:13,413 --> 00:15:16,024
The next time we
appear in court,

283
00:15:16,048 --> 00:15:17,960
kinda clean
yourself up a little bit

284
00:15:17,984 --> 00:15:20,920
and try to get some
different clothes, got it?

285
00:15:31,998 --> 00:15:34,024
Yeah, I got it.

286
00:15:38,037 --> 00:15:39,982
So why you are
representing the little creep?

287
00:15:40,006 --> 00:15:43,018
Uh, it's, uh, it's personal.

288
00:15:43,042 --> 00:15:46,088
So you were mad
at, uh... what was...?

289
00:15:46,112 --> 00:15:47,356
- Nicky.
- Yeah.

290
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:48,991
Yeah, I was mad at
him. As a matter of fact,

291
00:15:49,015 --> 00:15:50,526
if Gary and Renee
hadn't been there,

292
00:15:50,550 --> 00:15:51,960
I'd probably
punched his lights out.

293
00:15:51,984 --> 00:15:53,996
- How come?
- He lied to me.

294
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:56,398
He said that if I gaffed
four pictures for him,

295
00:15:56,422 --> 00:15:58,133
he'd let me direct.

296
00:15:58,157 --> 00:15:59,635
Then, after doing it,

297
00:15:59,659 --> 00:16:02,638
found out he'd been pumping
sunshine up my you know what.

298
00:16:02,662 --> 00:16:05,826
Is that why you weren't at
the premiere that next night?

299
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:08,377
How do you know I wasn't there?

300
00:16:08,401 --> 00:16:11,280
Well, your-your name
was on the guest list,

301
00:16:11,304 --> 00:16:13,749
but you never
picked up your ticket.

302
00:16:14,907 --> 00:16:17,186
Well, last thing I
wanted to do was look

303
00:16:17,210 --> 00:16:19,488
at that little geek
for two hours.

304
00:16:19,512 --> 00:16:20,512
Mm.

305
00:16:22,715 --> 00:16:26,929
So, uh... what did you do?

306
00:16:26,953 --> 00:16:28,063
I stayed at home.

307
00:16:28,087 --> 00:16:29,798
You got a family?

308
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:31,467
I'm divorced.

309
00:16:31,491 --> 00:16:33,936
Oh. So you were,
you were by yourself.

310
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:35,971
That night I was, yeah.

311
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:37,473
Huh.

312
00:16:38,598 --> 00:16:39,641
Does that hurt?

313
00:16:39,665 --> 00:16:41,643
Use it or lose it.

314
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:42,678
Yeah.

315
00:16:42,702 --> 00:16:44,379
Careful over there!

316
00:16:44,403 --> 00:16:46,782
Looks like you lost it.

317
00:16:46,806 --> 00:16:49,685
Yeah.

318
00:16:49,709 --> 00:16:53,388
Yeah, you lose it in my line
of work, and you're history.

319
00:16:53,412 --> 00:16:55,090
Speaking of history,

320
00:16:55,114 --> 00:16:59,995
I hear you did all that
incredible motorcycle stunt work

321
00:17:00,019 --> 00:17:01,864
in <i>Daredevil's Alley.</i>

322
00:17:01,888 --> 00:17:03,365
Yeah, that was me.

323
00:17:03,389 --> 00:17:05,868
I don't do bike work anymore.

324
00:17:05,892 --> 00:17:07,970
- It's too dangerous.
- Yeah.

325
00:17:07,994 --> 00:17:10,239
Yeah, I imagine it is.

326
00:17:10,263 --> 00:17:12,941
Yeah, I guess...
Yeah, I guess would be.

327
00:17:12,965 --> 00:17:13,989
Yeah, that...

328
00:17:31,384 --> 00:17:34,183
Around the side there.

329
00:17:37,356 --> 00:17:40,903
Look, the star is dead,
so the picture's dead.

330
00:17:40,927 --> 00:17:42,804
What can I tell you?

331
00:17:42,828 --> 00:17:45,407
Call my secretary when
you get back to L.A.

332
00:17:45,431 --> 00:17:46,909
We'll do lunch, okay?

333
00:17:46,933 --> 00:17:49,945
Yeah, all right, ciao. Ciao.

334
00:17:49,969 --> 00:17:52,548
Jackie! Yo, Jack.

335
00:17:52,572 --> 00:17:54,816
You want to tell your
guys that the picture's over?

336
00:17:54,840 --> 00:17:56,285
No goldbricking!

337
00:17:56,309 --> 00:17:59,788
I said no overtime
and I mean it!

338
00:17:59,812 --> 00:18:01,089
- Come on.
- Mr. Benton?

339
00:18:01,113 --> 00:18:02,858
Who are you?

340
00:18:02,882 --> 00:18:04,660
Conrad McMasters.
I'm a private investigator.

341
00:18:04,684 --> 00:18:06,361
I'm not interested.

342
00:18:06,385 --> 00:18:07,496
Excuse me?

343
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:08,964
PI's are box office poison.

344
00:18:08,988 --> 00:18:10,299
Try one of the networks.

345
00:18:10,323 --> 00:18:14,202
I work for Ben Matlock,
Cliff Lockwood's attorney.

346
00:18:14,226 --> 00:18:15,804
I need to ask you some
questions if I could, please.

347
00:18:15,828 --> 00:18:17,839
Oh!

348
00:18:17,863 --> 00:18:19,274
I'm sorry.

349
00:18:19,298 --> 00:18:21,777
People are always
coming up to me and trying

350
00:18:21,801 --> 00:18:23,679
to sell me the rights
to their life story:

351
00:18:23,703 --> 00:18:28,183
cops, doctors, teachers,
lawyers, dentists.

352
00:18:28,207 --> 00:18:31,119
Uh, I understand that you and
Nicky Tower used to argue a lot.

353
00:18:31,143 --> 00:18:33,689
We argued constantly!

354
00:18:33,713 --> 00:18:36,825
I'd budget something at
$20,000, he had to have $40,000.

355
00:18:36,849 --> 00:18:39,828
I'd get him the $40,000,
suddenly he needed $80,000.

356
00:18:39,852 --> 00:18:42,097
It was one continuous battle.

357
00:18:42,121 --> 00:18:44,800
So, it wasn't, it wasn't
anything personal?

358
00:18:44,824 --> 00:18:46,835
No, no, no, of course not.

359
00:18:46,859 --> 00:18:50,072
No, Nicky and I... all things
considered... we got on famously.

360
00:18:50,096 --> 00:18:53,141
So then why didn't you go to
the premiere of his new movie?

361
00:18:53,165 --> 00:18:56,411
'Cause it wasn't <i>my</i> movie.

362
00:18:57,536 --> 00:18:59,748
I was only here to
prep <i>my</i> new picture.

363
00:18:59,772 --> 00:19:02,351
And what'd you do that night?

364
00:19:02,375 --> 00:19:04,286
Uh, I ate dinner at the hotel,

365
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:07,656
made some calls, read the
trades; you know, the usual.

366
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:10,926
Well, thank you for your time.

367
00:19:10,950 --> 00:19:12,260
Sure.

368
00:19:12,284 --> 00:19:14,796
Representing Cliff
Lockwood, huh?

369
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:16,465
I don't get it.

370
00:19:16,489 --> 00:19:18,133
Hey, you know, actually,

371
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:21,370
actually, a lot of the
experiences I've had

372
00:19:21,394 --> 00:19:22,771
would make a pretty good movie.

373
00:19:22,795 --> 00:19:24,306
If I could leave another...

374
00:19:24,330 --> 00:19:27,075
Ah! Buh-buh-bye-bye.

375
00:19:27,099 --> 00:19:30,331
Yeah. I'm sorry.

376
00:19:34,907 --> 00:19:37,719
<i>Of course he was
difficult; he was a star.</i>

377
00:19:37,743 --> 00:19:40,122
And stars aren't necessarily
on the same wavelength

378
00:19:40,146 --> 00:19:41,523
as the rest of us.

379
00:19:41,547 --> 00:19:43,258
That's what makes them special.

380
00:19:43,282 --> 00:19:46,728
Yeah, I hear he ran you ragged.

381
00:19:46,752 --> 00:19:47,796
Here you go.

382
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:50,465
That was my job. I didn't mind.

383
00:19:50,489 --> 00:19:52,467
Did you, did you know

384
00:19:52,491 --> 00:19:55,804
that he... he
promised Steve Miller

385
00:19:55,828 --> 00:19:58,540
a shot at a picture?

386
00:19:58,564 --> 00:20:00,242
Who told you that?

387
00:20:00,266 --> 00:20:01,877
Steve Miller.

388
00:20:01,901 --> 00:20:03,745
Nicky never did any such thing.

389
00:20:03,769 --> 00:20:06,615
I said he was
special, not stupid.

390
00:20:06,639 --> 00:20:11,086
I thought you said he
liked to do the unexpected.

391
00:20:11,110 --> 00:20:14,489
If you're trying to pin his
murder on Steve Miller,

392
00:20:14,513 --> 00:20:15,957
that is fine with me.

393
00:20:15,981 --> 00:20:18,026
I think the guy's
a first-class leech,

394
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:20,362
but we both know
your client killed Nicky.

395
00:20:20,386 --> 00:20:23,799
He's a bum,
Mr. Matlock, a loser.

396
00:20:23,823 --> 00:20:27,302
Back in my wilder days, I
had a boyfriend just like him.

397
00:20:27,326 --> 00:20:28,937
He was a biker.

398
00:20:28,961 --> 00:20:31,006
All he wanted to do
was ride his motorcycles

399
00:20:31,030 --> 00:20:32,407
and hang out with his buddies.

400
00:20:32,431 --> 00:20:37,913
He was lazy and shiftless
and violent, just like Cliff.

401
00:20:37,937 --> 00:20:41,169
I tried to warn Nicky, but
he wouldn't listen to me.

402
00:20:43,476 --> 00:20:45,775
Is this you?

403
00:20:50,182 --> 00:20:51,673
Yes.

404
00:20:53,953 --> 00:20:57,532
I, uh, I went into the theater

405
00:20:57,556 --> 00:20:59,735
to make some last-minute
seating changes

406
00:20:59,759 --> 00:21:02,070
when I heard the shots.

407
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:05,607
Actually, I didn't even know
that they were shots until...

408
00:21:05,631 --> 00:21:09,244
I came out a couple of minutes
later and I... I saw a body

409
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:10,964
lying on the ground.

410
00:21:12,404 --> 00:21:15,033
When I saw that it was Nicky...

411
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:21,805
I loved him, in case
you hadn't guessed.

412
00:21:40,232 --> 00:21:42,677
Hey.

413
00:21:42,701 --> 00:21:43,479
Got your message.

414
00:21:43,503 --> 00:21:44,480
What's up?

415
00:21:44,504 --> 00:21:47,415
Well, I don't know.

416
00:21:47,439 --> 00:21:50,152
Nobody I've talked
to has anything nice

417
00:21:50,176 --> 00:21:52,154
to say about our boy Cliff.

418
00:21:52,178 --> 00:21:53,455
Yeah, me, too.

419
00:21:53,479 --> 00:21:56,491
The call him bum, creep.

420
00:21:56,515 --> 00:21:59,795
One of 'em said right
out that he killed this, uh...

421
00:21:59,819 --> 00:22:01,296
- Nicky.
- Yeah, yeah.

422
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:06,268
But this Steve Miller lied about
the argument he had with Nicky

423
00:22:06,292 --> 00:22:07,769
the day before the murder.

424
00:22:07,793 --> 00:22:09,604
His alibi isn't
very good either.

425
00:22:09,628 --> 00:22:11,706
So what are you
doing, following him?

426
00:22:11,730 --> 00:22:13,775
You don't think
it's a good idea?

427
00:22:13,799 --> 00:22:15,210
Yeah, okay, I'll take over.

428
00:22:15,234 --> 00:22:16,411
Where's he at, in
the bar over there?

429
00:22:16,435 --> 00:22:18,028
No, he's in the shop next to it.

430
00:22:19,138 --> 00:22:20,436
You gotta be kidding.

431
00:22:22,741 --> 00:22:24,386
No, wait! Ben, don't!

432
00:22:24,410 --> 00:22:26,054
No, Ben, no, no! Let
me drive, all right?

433
00:22:26,078 --> 00:22:27,355
Let me drive.

434
00:22:27,379 --> 00:22:28,957
- He's-He's-He's pulling out!
- Wait!

435
00:22:28,981 --> 00:22:31,259
Ben, you're not very
good at this. Don't!

436
00:23:00,412 --> 00:23:01,590
Who's that?

437
00:23:01,614 --> 00:23:02,991
- Ben, you're too close.
- No, I'm not.

438
00:23:03,015 --> 00:23:04,359
Yes, you are. He's
gonna see you.

439
00:23:04,383 --> 00:23:06,127
No, he won't.

440
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:07,262
He ju... He just did!

441
00:23:07,286 --> 00:23:09,264
I don't believe this!

442
00:23:09,288 --> 00:23:11,052
Oh!

443
00:23:12,591 --> 00:23:14,336
You following me?

444
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:16,171
Just want to ask you a
couple more questions.

445
00:23:16,195 --> 00:23:17,606
No way! Get out of here!

446
00:23:17,630 --> 00:23:19,241
Don't... don't I know
you from somewhere?

447
00:23:19,265 --> 00:23:20,542
Get back inside. Hurry up.

448
00:23:20,566 --> 00:23:22,177
No, wait. Didn't I see
you at the courthouse?

449
00:23:22,201 --> 00:23:23,712
Vicky, I said go back inside!

450
00:23:23,736 --> 00:23:26,205
You were at Cliff Lockwood's
hearing, weren't you?

451
00:23:27,339 --> 00:23:30,685
Were... STEVE: Damn it!

452
00:23:30,709 --> 00:23:32,921
I'm sorry, Daddy, I had to go.

453
00:23:32,945 --> 00:23:34,956
I had to see the
man who killed Nicky.

454
00:23:34,980 --> 00:23:36,157
This is your daughter?

455
00:23:36,181 --> 00:23:38,059
Why don't you just get lost?

456
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:39,661
You knew Nicky?

457
00:23:39,685 --> 00:23:43,031
Hey, you don't
have to answer him.

458
00:23:43,055 --> 00:23:44,699
Would you rather I subpoena her

459
00:23:44,723 --> 00:23:46,919
and have her
answer in open court?

460
00:23:48,894 --> 00:23:50,829
I was in love with him.

461
00:23:52,564 --> 00:23:54,658
He's the father.

462
00:23:59,238 --> 00:24:01,416
Why don't you...

463
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:05,605
uh, go inside, and we'll
see how that new blouse fits.

464
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:14,296
At first, she told me that it
was, uh, a boy from her school.

465
00:24:14,320 --> 00:24:17,132
And then when I
found out the truth,

466
00:24:17,156 --> 00:24:18,733
I wanted to kill
the little letch.

467
00:24:18,757 --> 00:24:21,136
But I didn't do it.

468
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:23,891
I was here visiting
Vicky when he got shot.

469
00:24:25,898 --> 00:24:27,876
Oh, why don't you ask her.

470
00:24:27,900 --> 00:24:29,892
It's her grandmother's house.

471
00:25:03,369 --> 00:25:05,361
Hi.

472
00:25:06,505 --> 00:25:07,849
Hi.

473
00:25:07,873 --> 00:25:11,186
Me and the homeboys are
gonna take a little road trip.

474
00:25:11,210 --> 00:25:12,754
Just wanted to say good-bye.

475
00:25:12,778 --> 00:25:14,456
When you coming back?

476
00:25:14,480 --> 00:25:16,958
I'm not.

477
00:25:16,982 --> 00:25:18,426
I don't stand a
snowball's chance in hell

478
00:25:18,450 --> 00:25:19,728
in that courtroom,
and you know it.

479
00:25:19,752 --> 00:25:22,764
You don't stand a
snowball's chance in hell

480
00:25:22,788 --> 00:25:24,188
if you leave.

481
00:25:26,225 --> 00:25:30,205
Well, thanks to you and
my old man for all your help.

482
00:25:30,229 --> 00:25:33,222
He and your justice system
are perfect for each other.

483
00:25:35,267 --> 00:25:37,278
I gotta tell you something.

484
00:25:37,302 --> 00:25:40,081
I don't give a merry
damn what you do.

485
00:25:40,105 --> 00:25:41,916
Good.

486
00:25:41,940 --> 00:25:46,921
You leave... you got no chance!

487
00:25:46,945 --> 00:25:50,125
You stay, you
might have a chance.

488
00:25:50,149 --> 00:25:54,462
A chance at what,
going to prison?

489
00:25:54,486 --> 00:25:56,216
That ain't gonna happen.

490
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:14,904
Good riddance.

491
00:26:19,978 --> 00:26:21,056
<i>He just took off?</i>

492
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:24,726
<i>Like a bat</i> out of hell,
as the saying goes.

493
00:26:24,750 --> 00:26:25,894
You talk to his father?

494
00:26:25,918 --> 00:26:27,328
Yep.

495
00:26:27,352 --> 00:26:29,731
He said if I dropped the
case, he'd understand.

496
00:26:29,755 --> 00:26:32,167
Are you going to?

497
00:26:32,191 --> 00:26:34,369
Oh, yeah.

498
00:26:34,393 --> 00:26:36,171
But if you drop the case,
he's gonna go through

499
00:26:36,195 --> 00:26:37,772
the rest of his life
thinking he was right.

500
00:26:37,796 --> 00:26:40,208
About his father,
about the system...

501
00:26:40,232 --> 00:26:42,377
about you.

502
00:26:42,401 --> 00:26:44,734
Well...

503
00:26:46,738 --> 00:26:50,118
Oh... Haven't you
ever been wild?

504
00:26:50,142 --> 00:26:52,475
No, not much.

505
00:26:54,513 --> 00:26:55,657
Mama wouldn't let me.

506
00:26:56,682 --> 00:26:57,725
I'm glad.

507
00:26:57,749 --> 00:27:00,261
Well, I have.

508
00:27:00,285 --> 00:27:02,163
I used to get drunked up, fight.

509
00:27:02,187 --> 00:27:03,798
I had a bike.

510
00:27:03,822 --> 00:27:04,799
Jail?

511
00:27:04,823 --> 00:27:05,967
Yeah.

512
00:27:05,991 --> 00:27:07,168
Fight and disorderly.

513
00:27:07,192 --> 00:27:10,138
What turned you around?

514
00:27:10,162 --> 00:27:14,142
My father told me if I didn't
stop my troublemaking,

515
00:27:14,166 --> 00:27:16,744
I was gonna wind up in
a place worse than hell.

516
00:27:16,768 --> 00:27:18,146
He told me he loved me,

517
00:27:18,170 --> 00:27:20,915
he cared about me... Yeah?

518
00:27:20,939 --> 00:27:24,352
Yeah, then he hit me right
here as hard as he could.

519
00:27:25,410 --> 00:27:26,621
And then what?

520
00:27:26,645 --> 00:27:29,457
I saw... the man knew
what he was talking about.

521
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:31,726
Yeah.

522
00:27:32,784 --> 00:27:34,462
So what are you gonna do?

523
00:27:34,486 --> 00:27:37,398
I don't know.

524
00:27:37,422 --> 00:27:39,167
Don't know.

525
00:27:39,191 --> 00:27:40,702
Case is only a
couple of days away.

526
00:27:40,726 --> 00:27:41,903
Could be in Mexico, Ben.

527
00:27:41,927 --> 00:27:43,919
Yeah.

528
00:27:47,766 --> 00:27:52,101
Well... maybe you
better get going.

529
00:27:56,241 --> 00:27:57,252
Oh, oh, oh.

530
00:27:57,276 --> 00:27:59,554
By the way, Gary Benton wasn't

531
00:27:59,578 --> 00:28:01,556
in his motel room the
night of the murder.

532
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:04,359
A parking attendant
remembers bringing his car up

533
00:28:04,383 --> 00:28:07,495
at 5:30 and then parking it
for him an hour or so later.

534
00:28:07,519 --> 00:28:09,764
Huh.

535
00:28:09,788 --> 00:28:11,689
You know where he went?

536
00:28:12,791 --> 00:28:14,536
You got a motive?

537
00:28:14,560 --> 00:28:17,739
The word is that the film
that Gary was prepping

538
00:28:17,763 --> 00:28:19,707
was a surefire bomb.

539
00:28:19,731 --> 00:28:22,477
Evidently, Nicky Tower took
a script that everyone loved

540
00:28:22,501 --> 00:28:25,246
and then rewrote it until
it was a piece of garbage.

541
00:28:27,139 --> 00:28:29,784
You think that's what all the
arguments were really about?

542
00:28:29,808 --> 00:28:32,086
Uh-huh. According to the
crew, this film was so bad

543
00:28:32,110 --> 00:28:33,521
that if it had been released,

544
00:28:33,545 --> 00:28:35,256
it would've destroyed
Gary's career.

545
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:37,525
Well, I'll be dogged.

546
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:38,726
Huh.

547
00:28:38,750 --> 00:28:40,562
We'll have to keep
that one in mind.

548
00:28:44,056 --> 00:28:45,033
I'll see you.

549
00:28:45,057 --> 00:28:46,855
Yeah...

550
00:28:53,999 --> 00:28:55,143
You know, you're right.

551
00:28:55,167 --> 00:28:56,945
I don't think I was in my hotel.

552
00:28:56,969 --> 00:28:59,681
Oh, I was out getting dinner.

553
00:28:59,705 --> 00:29:00,682
Where?

554
00:29:00,706 --> 00:29:02,884
Uh, I don't remember right off.

555
00:29:03,909 --> 00:29:05,386
I go to a lot of places.

556
00:29:05,410 --> 00:29:07,855
You know, I'm still looking for a
decent restaurant around here.

557
00:29:07,879 --> 00:29:09,123
Oh.

558
00:29:09,147 --> 00:29:12,126
I can't wait till this
trial thing is over,

559
00:29:12,150 --> 00:29:13,895
so I can get back to L.A.

560
00:29:13,919 --> 00:29:14,896
Yeah.

561
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:16,998
Uh...

562
00:29:17,022 --> 00:29:19,601
what-what, uh, what
happened to the, uh, movie

563
00:29:19,625 --> 00:29:20,835
you came here to produce?

564
00:29:20,859 --> 00:29:21,836
Defunct.

565
00:29:21,860 --> 00:29:24,072
It was tailor-made
for Nicky Tower.

566
00:29:24,096 --> 00:29:27,175
With him gone,
studios aren't interested.

567
00:29:27,199 --> 00:29:29,410
I hear it was
gonna be a stinker.

568
00:29:29,434 --> 00:29:30,979
W-Well...

569
00:29:31,003 --> 00:29:33,514
well, it wasn't gonna win
any Oscars, that's for sure.

570
00:29:33,538 --> 00:29:34,716
But, uh...

571
00:29:34,740 --> 00:29:36,351
But it worked out
for the best, didn't it?

572
00:29:36,375 --> 00:29:39,020
I mean, the studio
had Nicky insured

573
00:29:39,044 --> 00:29:41,689
and you're out from under
a project that might have

574
00:29:41,713 --> 00:29:44,492
made you a laughingstock
back in, uh, Hollywood.

575
00:29:44,516 --> 00:29:47,295
Ida Clayton, please
pick up the house phone.

576
00:29:47,319 --> 00:29:50,298
Nicky Tower may have been
a pain in the neck, Mr. Matlock,

577
00:29:50,322 --> 00:29:51,966
but he was a friend of mine.

578
00:29:51,990 --> 00:29:54,469
And his death was
a great loss to me.

579
00:29:54,493 --> 00:29:57,205
In fact, I shouldn't be talking
to anybody but my shrink,

580
00:29:57,229 --> 00:29:59,340
so if-if you don't mind, I'd...

581
00:29:59,364 --> 00:30:01,709
W-Well, wait a minute,
wait a minute, wait a minute.

582
00:30:01,733 --> 00:30:06,881
I-I found a biographical
sketch on you in the library.

583
00:30:06,905 --> 00:30:08,783
Uh-huh.

584
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:12,642
Did you know that you're in
<i>Who's Who in the Film Industry?</i>

585
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:15,923
Of course I am.

586
00:30:15,947 --> 00:30:18,893
And-and-and the sketch said that

587
00:30:18,917 --> 00:30:21,978
one of your hobbies
is racing motorcycles.

588
00:30:23,021 --> 00:30:24,632
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

589
00:30:26,124 --> 00:30:29,537
Well, the guy that does my
publicity tends to exaggerate.

590
00:30:29,561 --> 00:30:31,572
I don't race them, I ride them.

591
00:30:31,596 --> 00:30:33,374
- Uh-huh...
- Occasionally.

592
00:30:33,398 --> 00:30:35,958
And only the little ones.

593
00:30:38,003 --> 00:30:40,415
The success motivation seminar

594
00:30:40,439 --> 00:30:41,849
will be taking place at

595
00:30:41,873 --> 00:30:44,652
7:00 p.m. tonight
in the Empire Room.

596
00:30:44,676 --> 00:30:46,454
The seminar is
open to the public,

597
00:30:46,478 --> 00:30:50,391
and details are available
at the concierge desk.

598
00:30:50,415 --> 00:30:53,061
Why don't we ask
that girl to join us?

599
00:30:53,085 --> 00:30:54,662
What do you mean?

600
00:30:54,686 --> 00:30:56,197
That girl.

601
00:30:56,221 --> 00:30:58,499
Hi!

602
00:30:58,523 --> 00:31:00,435
I'd rather not.

603
00:31:02,194 --> 00:31:05,858
You want me to talk
with her by myself?

604
00:31:10,902 --> 00:31:13,314
You want to know where I
was when Nicky was murdered?

605
00:31:13,338 --> 00:31:16,317
I was with her.

606
00:31:16,341 --> 00:31:17,719
She was upset.

607
00:31:17,743 --> 00:31:22,939
You see, Nicky...
got a little kinky.

608
00:31:25,984 --> 00:31:28,463
H-How upset was she?

609
00:31:28,487 --> 00:31:31,265
She said she was
going to sell her story

610
00:31:31,289 --> 00:31:32,400
to the <i>National Informer.</i>

611
00:31:32,424 --> 00:31:34,402
Ooh. Ooh.

612
00:31:34,426 --> 00:31:36,918
So you paid her off, huh?

613
00:31:38,063 --> 00:31:39,474
Look, you're not,
you're not gonna

614
00:31:39,498 --> 00:31:40,808
tell anybody
about this, are you?

615
00:31:40,832 --> 00:31:43,544
I mean, the public adored Nicky.

616
00:31:43,568 --> 00:31:45,980
People would be
devastated if they found out.

617
00:31:46,004 --> 00:31:49,016
And it wouldn't
exactly do wonders

618
00:31:49,040 --> 00:31:50,485
for my reputation either.

619
00:31:50,509 --> 00:31:53,287
I-I don't understand something.

620
00:31:53,311 --> 00:31:54,722
Why didn't you just quit?

621
00:31:54,746 --> 00:31:57,925
Because they were
paying me $875,000

622
00:31:57,949 --> 00:31:59,260
plus two percent of the gross.

623
00:31:59,284 --> 00:32:00,828
Oh.

624
00:32:09,895 --> 00:32:11,072
Ben, it's me.

625
00:32:11,096 --> 00:32:12,573
Hi. Any luck?

626
00:32:12,597 --> 00:32:13,941
Yeah. I'm in a bar

627
00:32:13,965 --> 00:32:15,877
on Highway 53
just south of Griffin

628
00:32:15,901 --> 00:32:16,878
called The Corral.

629
00:32:16,902 --> 00:32:17,879
Cliff and his pals are inside.

630
00:32:17,903 --> 00:32:18,946
Don't let him leave.

631
00:32:18,970 --> 00:32:20,410
What do you mean
don't let him leave?

632
00:32:21,673 --> 00:32:23,665
Hello?

633
00:32:28,814 --> 00:32:30,806
It's all yours.

634
00:32:44,596 --> 00:32:46,908
Who's going with me now?

635
00:32:46,932 --> 00:32:49,343
Huh? Oh, baby.

636
00:32:49,367 --> 00:32:51,359
Who's coming with me?

637
00:33:07,819 --> 00:33:09,811
That guy, uh, right there...

638
00:33:17,095 --> 00:33:18,072
All right.

639
00:33:18,096 --> 00:33:19,707
Give them up.

640
00:33:19,731 --> 00:33:21,075
What are you talking about?

641
00:33:21,099 --> 00:33:22,710
My plug wires, that's
what I'm talking about!

642
00:33:22,734 --> 00:33:24,145
- I don't have them.
- Where are they?

643
00:33:24,169 --> 00:33:26,013
- What are you talking about?
- Get him, Sonny.

644
00:33:26,037 --> 00:33:27,415
Get him out of there.
Quick, get him out of there.

645
00:33:27,439 --> 00:33:29,584
You don't mess with a
man's bike, you hear me?!

646
00:33:29,608 --> 00:33:31,986
You don't mess
with a man's bike!

647
00:33:32,010 --> 00:33:32,987
Think about it, man!

648
00:33:33,011 --> 00:33:34,388
If I find you, so will the cops!

649
00:33:34,412 --> 00:33:35,590
Oh, yeah?

650
00:33:38,483 --> 00:33:41,262
Teach you not to
mess with a man's bike.

651
00:33:44,222 --> 00:33:45,967
Look out.

652
00:33:45,991 --> 00:33:47,101
Get out of the way!

653
00:33:49,561 --> 00:33:51,873
Well, look who's here.

654
00:33:51,897 --> 00:33:53,889
Easy, easy.

655
00:33:55,901 --> 00:33:57,345
- Watch it!
- Hey!

656
00:33:57,369 --> 00:34:00,147
Watch it!

657
00:34:00,171 --> 00:34:01,616
Get in the car.

658
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:03,584
I'm not going
nowhere with you, man.

659
00:34:03,608 --> 00:34:05,620
Either you go
with me in that car

660
00:34:05,644 --> 00:34:08,356
or you go to prison
with the cops in theirs.

661
00:34:08,380 --> 00:34:10,758
That courtroom crap of yours
doesn't work for people like me.

662
00:34:10,782 --> 00:34:12,326
Get in the car!

663
00:34:12,350 --> 00:34:13,895
You just leave me alone.

664
00:34:13,919 --> 00:34:15,751
Quit acting stupid
and get in the car!

665
00:34:17,789 --> 00:34:18,766
Stupid?

666
00:34:18,790 --> 00:34:20,301
Yeah, stupid!

667
00:34:20,325 --> 00:34:21,936
You're getting
back at your father

668
00:34:21,960 --> 00:34:24,772
and everything he
represents... Law, reason.

669
00:34:24,796 --> 00:34:26,774
That's your problem.

670
00:34:26,798 --> 00:34:28,643
Whether you killed
that fella or not,

671
00:34:28,667 --> 00:34:32,480
unless you face trial, you're
going to prison surer than hell.

672
00:34:32,504 --> 00:34:36,032
I don't know what you call
that, but I call that stupid!

673
00:34:39,010 --> 00:34:41,055
How do I know
you can get me off?

674
00:34:41,079 --> 00:34:42,690
You don't.

675
00:34:42,714 --> 00:34:45,760
But I'm the only shot
you got right now.

676
00:34:45,784 --> 00:34:46,808
Get in the car.

677
00:34:48,486 --> 00:34:50,478
Get in the car!

678
00:35:24,823 --> 00:35:26,467
<i>Right now, I do believe
Nicky has arrived!</i>

679
00:35:26,491 --> 00:35:28,135
<i>As you can tell from
the crowd reaction.</i>

680
00:35:28,159 --> 00:35:29,937
People taking pictures
for their photo albums.

681
00:35:29,961 --> 00:35:31,339
- Here you go.
- We're gonna see

682
00:35:31,363 --> 00:35:33,341
if we can get a word
with Nicky right now.

683
00:35:33,365 --> 00:35:34,942
If we can get in here...

684
00:35:36,735 --> 00:35:37,712
Ben.

685
00:35:37,736 --> 00:35:38,846
- In here.
- Oh, my God,

686
00:35:38,870 --> 00:35:40,214
did you see that?
Someone just rode by

687
00:35:40,238 --> 00:35:41,882
- on a motorcycle...
- Hey.

688
00:35:41,906 --> 00:35:43,551
How about a nice, fresh

689
00:35:43,575 --> 00:35:45,920
piece of hot apple pie?

690
00:35:45,944 --> 00:35:47,254
Oh, great!

691
00:35:48,313 --> 00:35:49,657
Thanks.

692
00:35:49,681 --> 00:35:51,377
How'd you know I'd still be up?

693
00:35:53,318 --> 00:35:56,530
The trial's in two days; you
don't know who the killer is...

694
00:35:56,554 --> 00:35:59,767
I knew you'd be up.

695
00:35:59,791 --> 00:36:01,869
I got a notion.

696
00:36:01,893 --> 00:36:03,738
Just a notion?

697
00:36:03,762 --> 00:36:06,741
Well, it's pretty good though.

698
00:36:06,765 --> 00:36:08,576
Are you gonna tell me?

699
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:11,178
- What?
- What the notion is.

700
00:36:11,202 --> 00:36:14,281
Oh, my God!

701
00:36:14,305 --> 00:36:16,706
Look at that.

702
00:36:18,043 --> 00:36:19,220
Get in here.

703
00:36:21,246 --> 00:36:23,147
Why didn't I see that before?

704
00:36:24,182 --> 00:36:26,193
We've still got two days.

705
00:36:26,217 --> 00:36:28,029
Huh. Great.

706
00:36:28,053 --> 00:36:29,646
Yeah.

707
00:36:38,730 --> 00:36:41,222
All right, man, how do I look?

708
00:36:47,005 --> 00:36:49,804
You look like a winner.

709
00:36:51,843 --> 00:36:53,505
Well?

710
00:37:00,552 --> 00:37:02,563
Yes, that's right.

711
00:37:02,587 --> 00:37:05,599
I sold him a bike
just like that one.

712
00:37:05,623 --> 00:37:08,069
A Claymore 1200 Hyperglide.

713
00:37:08,093 --> 00:37:10,271
Thank you, Mr. Bonzer.

714
00:37:10,295 --> 00:37:12,506
Your witness.

715
00:37:12,530 --> 00:37:14,742
Uh, Mr. Bonzer...

716
00:37:14,766 --> 00:37:18,846
I'm going to show you
something, uh, which we'll identify

717
00:37:18,870 --> 00:37:21,482
as Defense Exhibit K,

718
00:37:21,506 --> 00:37:24,151
and which the
prosecution has stipulated

719
00:37:24,175 --> 00:37:27,421
belongs to my client.

720
00:37:27,445 --> 00:37:31,792
His Claymore 1200
Hyperglide motorcycle.

721
00:37:34,786 --> 00:37:36,097
Yeah!

722
00:37:38,723 --> 00:37:40,534
Objection!

723
00:37:40,558 --> 00:37:42,970
- What?
- Objection!

724
00:37:42,994 --> 00:37:44,572
Mr. Matlock!

725
00:37:44,596 --> 00:37:46,574
Have him turn that thing off!

726
00:37:46,598 --> 00:37:48,642
Hey, Chester! Turn it off!

727
00:37:49,701 --> 00:37:51,479
Your Honor,

728
00:37:51,503 --> 00:37:54,148
I object... to these
cheap theatrics.

729
00:37:54,172 --> 00:37:56,117
Well, you said I could

730
00:37:56,141 --> 00:37:58,285
bring the motorcycle
in the courtroom.

731
00:37:58,309 --> 00:38:01,589
I said bring it
in, not ride it in!

732
00:38:01,613 --> 00:38:05,359
Your Honor, I... I
apologize for-for the noise,

733
00:38:05,383 --> 00:38:09,597
but I-I had to do it in order
to get my next point across.

734
00:38:09,621 --> 00:38:11,465
All right.

735
00:38:11,489 --> 00:38:12,867
Proceed.

736
00:38:12,891 --> 00:38:14,802
Oh, thank you.

737
00:38:14,826 --> 00:38:17,371
Now, Mr., Mr. Bonzer,

738
00:38:17,395 --> 00:38:20,007
why is this bike so noisy?

739
00:38:20,031 --> 00:38:21,675
You got dual exhaust.

740
00:38:21,699 --> 00:38:25,479
Dual exhaust. D... Oh. Yes.

741
00:38:25,503 --> 00:38:26,981
Two exhausts.

742
00:38:27,005 --> 00:38:30,050
There's one right
here and one right here.

743
00:38:30,074 --> 00:38:32,119
Yeah. Yeah, two.

744
00:38:32,143 --> 00:38:33,621
Now...

745
00:38:33,645 --> 00:38:36,190
how-how... that's the bike
the murderer was riding.

746
00:38:36,214 --> 00:38:37,458
How many...

747
00:38:37,482 --> 00:38:41,362
how many exhaust pipes
on... on that motorcycle?

748
00:38:41,386 --> 00:38:42,830
I can't tell from that angle.

749
00:38:42,854 --> 00:38:44,365
Uh-huh. Okay, how about here?

750
00:38:44,389 --> 00:38:47,001
Fast-forward, yeah.

751
00:38:47,025 --> 00:38:48,960
That angle.

752
00:38:51,496 --> 00:38:54,141
- Single exhaust.
- Single exhaust.

753
00:38:54,165 --> 00:38:59,146
In other words, the bike
my client owns is not the bike

754
00:38:59,170 --> 00:39:03,317
the person who shot Nicky
Tower is riding after all, is it?

755
00:39:03,341 --> 00:39:05,286
Nope, it sure isn't.

756
00:39:05,310 --> 00:39:07,142
Thank you.

757
00:39:08,479 --> 00:39:10,958
Cross?

758
00:39:10,982 --> 00:39:14,628
Mr. Bonzer, isn't it
possible that Mr. Lockwood

759
00:39:14,652 --> 00:39:18,399
could have installed those
dual pipes after the murder?

760
00:39:18,423 --> 00:39:20,634
- Nope.
- Why not?

761
00:39:20,658 --> 00:39:23,070
'Cause I installed
them pipes myself

762
00:39:23,094 --> 00:39:25,539
a good six weeks
before the murder.

763
00:39:25,563 --> 00:39:27,395
Oh.

764
00:39:30,201 --> 00:39:32,313
The prosecution
rests, Your Honor.

765
00:39:33,605 --> 00:39:35,983
Mr. Matlock, call
your first witness.

766
00:39:36,007 --> 00:39:39,637
Uh, defense calls Ms.
Renee Williams to the stand.

767
00:39:40,678 --> 00:39:42,271
You may be seated.

768
00:39:44,749 --> 00:39:47,728
Uh, wh-when you learned

769
00:39:47,752 --> 00:39:51,065
that my client didn't have
any liability insurance,

770
00:39:51,089 --> 00:39:53,801
you insisted that he
get some, didn't you?

771
00:39:53,825 --> 00:39:55,536
Yes. Well, he wasn't exactly

772
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:57,471
what I would call a
responsible citizen.

773
00:39:57,495 --> 00:40:00,040
I didn't want Mr. Tower
to wind up getting sued

774
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:01,141
for an accident which

775
00:40:01,165 --> 00:40:02,810
- your client had caused.
- Mm-hmm.

776
00:40:02,834 --> 00:40:04,345
Who paid for the policy?

777
00:40:04,369 --> 00:40:05,779
Mr. Tower did.

778
00:40:05,803 --> 00:40:07,514
Who did the actual paperwork?

779
00:40:07,538 --> 00:40:10,084
I did. Handling his
financial matters

780
00:40:10,108 --> 00:40:12,019
- was part of my job.
- Mm-hmm.

781
00:40:12,043 --> 00:40:16,257
My client had to describe
his motorcycle in every detail

782
00:40:16,281 --> 00:40:18,959
on that insurance form
application, didn't he?

783
00:40:18,983 --> 00:40:21,829
- I believe so, yes.
- Yeah.

784
00:40:21,853 --> 00:40:23,664
You took...

785
00:40:23,688 --> 00:40:26,333
that description to a
shop down in Macon

786
00:40:26,357 --> 00:40:27,968
the day before the murder

787
00:40:27,992 --> 00:40:31,071
so you could rent a bike
exactly like his, didn't you?

788
00:40:31,095 --> 00:40:33,207
I did no such thing, no.

789
00:40:33,231 --> 00:40:36,076
Of course, you didn't use
your real name, you paid cash,

790
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:39,280
wore big sunglasses and
a red wig, but that was you

791
00:40:39,304 --> 00:40:42,349
that rented a Claymore
1200 Hyperglide motorcycle

792
00:40:42,373 --> 00:40:45,252
from Rory's Motorcycle
Shop on the 19th,

793
00:40:45,276 --> 00:40:47,888
and returned it on the
21st, wasn't it, Ms. Williams?

794
00:40:47,912 --> 00:40:49,556
- No, it wasn't.
- Course...

795
00:40:49,580 --> 00:40:51,992
course there's...
one-one thing happened.

796
00:40:52,016 --> 00:40:56,563
My client put those dual
exhausts on after he filled out

797
00:40:56,587 --> 00:40:57,998
the application form.

798
00:40:58,022 --> 00:41:01,356
See, that's unfortunately
a little detail you missed.

799
00:41:02,593 --> 00:41:05,673
I have no idea what
you're talking about.

800
00:41:05,697 --> 00:41:10,077
You insisted he register
all his firearms, didn't you?

801
00:41:10,101 --> 00:41:11,478
Yes.

802
00:41:11,502 --> 00:41:13,681
So you knew he had a gun.

803
00:41:13,705 --> 00:41:15,149
Well, yes, but...

804
00:41:15,173 --> 00:41:18,352
You could've stolen that
gun, shot Nicky Tower with it,

805
00:41:18,376 --> 00:41:20,621
and everybody would
think my client had done it.

806
00:41:20,645 --> 00:41:21,922
- That is not true.
- Objection!

807
00:41:21,946 --> 00:41:23,090
This is pure speculation.

808
00:41:23,114 --> 00:41:25,826
Mr. Matlock has yet
to prove any of this.

809
00:41:25,850 --> 00:41:28,295
Sustained. Mr. Matlock,
I strongly suggest

810
00:41:28,319 --> 00:41:30,664
you move on with
another line of questioning.

811
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:34,134
Uh, yes, sir. Boy, that's
a beautiful bracelet.

812
00:41:34,158 --> 00:41:35,669
Ooh, look at that.

813
00:41:35,693 --> 00:41:36,837
Whew!

814
00:41:36,861 --> 00:41:38,706
Nicky Tower gave
you that, didn't he?

815
00:41:38,730 --> 00:41:40,975
Yes, he did.

816
00:41:40,999 --> 00:41:44,712
And-and-and on the underside,
there's an inscription, says...

817
00:41:44,736 --> 00:41:50,351
says: "T-To my only love,
with love forever. Nicky."

818
00:41:50,375 --> 00:41:51,707
Right?

819
00:41:52,744 --> 00:41:54,154
- Yes, there-there is.
- Yeah.

820
00:41:54,178 --> 00:41:55,456
There is.

821
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:58,625
He gave a bracelet just
like that to somebody else.

822
00:41:58,649 --> 00:42:03,897
And we traced it to a
jeweler in Los Angeles.

823
00:42:03,921 --> 00:42:05,265
Nicky Tower bought

824
00:42:05,289 --> 00:42:08,691
not one, not two, but
12 of those bracelets.

825
00:42:12,030 --> 00:42:15,228
You were in love
with him, weren't you?

826
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:20,581
Yes, I was.

827
00:42:21,939 --> 00:42:26,520
My client overheard
the fight you had with him

828
00:42:26,544 --> 00:42:28,655
when the bill for
those bracelets

829
00:42:28,679 --> 00:42:32,893
accidentally came
across your desk.

830
00:42:32,917 --> 00:42:35,929
You were furious, weren't you?

831
00:42:35,953 --> 00:42:38,932
And when you heard
the two of them fighting...

832
00:42:38,956 --> 00:42:40,768
My client and Nicky Tower...

833
00:42:40,792 --> 00:42:44,371
You rented that
motorcycle, stole his gun,

834
00:42:44,395 --> 00:42:46,507
waited in the alley the
night of the premiere

835
00:42:46,531 --> 00:42:48,208
until the right moment,

836
00:42:48,232 --> 00:42:50,677
then roared by
on that motorcycle,

837
00:42:50,701 --> 00:42:52,813
shot Nicky Tower
three times, rode it into

838
00:42:52,837 --> 00:42:55,516
the back of a waiting
van parked in a garage,

839
00:42:55,540 --> 00:42:57,551
changed as quickly as possible,

840
00:42:57,575 --> 00:43:00,254
got back down to the
street, over the body,

841
00:43:00,278 --> 00:43:02,990
so you could have your
picture in the paper, all...

842
00:43:03,014 --> 00:43:04,958
- for revenge.
- No!

843
00:43:04,982 --> 00:43:06,994
Your Honor, Your
Honor, he's doing it again.

844
00:43:07,018 --> 00:43:10,364
Mr. Matlock seems incapable
of telling the difference

845
00:43:10,388 --> 00:43:12,880
between conjecture and proof.

846
00:43:16,360 --> 00:43:19,239
I-I have proof, Your Honor.

847
00:43:19,263 --> 00:43:21,542
Overruled.

848
00:43:21,566 --> 00:43:25,379
There were, uh, a
lot of photographers

849
00:43:25,403 --> 00:43:27,414
taking a lot of
pictures that night.

850
00:43:27,438 --> 00:43:31,185
Among them... Robby
Atkins, there in the front row.

851
00:43:31,209 --> 00:43:34,354
See? There he is on the screen.

852
00:43:34,378 --> 00:43:36,090
He was trying out a...

853
00:43:36,114 --> 00:43:41,028
a new telephoto camera
his uncle had given him.

854
00:43:41,052 --> 00:43:46,400
And... according to these...

855
00:43:46,424 --> 00:43:51,705
This is... This here
is-is... blowups...

856
00:43:51,729 --> 00:43:53,707
of one of those pictures.

857
00:43:53,731 --> 00:43:55,976
Pass those around.

858
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:58,545
There you go, sir.

859
00:43:58,569 --> 00:44:00,814
And as you can see...

860
00:44:00,838 --> 00:44:03,183
that lens did beautifully.

861
00:44:03,207 --> 00:44:05,552
I mean, even in blowup here,

862
00:44:05,576 --> 00:44:08,355
the image is razor-sharp.

863
00:44:08,379 --> 00:44:10,290
It is so sharp...

864
00:44:10,314 --> 00:44:12,659
that you can see the reflection

865
00:44:12,683 --> 00:44:15,429
in-in the window in the
building across the street

866
00:44:15,453 --> 00:44:18,398
of a person sitting
astride a motorcycle

867
00:44:18,422 --> 00:44:20,734
in the alley next
to the theater.

868
00:44:20,758 --> 00:44:23,303
It's the killer...

869
00:44:23,327 --> 00:44:28,108
just before she
puts... her helmet on.

870
00:44:28,132 --> 00:44:30,477
Look here. Look, look.

871
00:44:30,501 --> 00:44:33,113
You can even see
the gun in her hand.

872
00:44:33,137 --> 00:44:35,231
See it there, right
by the helmet?

873
00:44:41,078 --> 00:44:45,276
That is you... isn't
it, Ms. Williams?

874
00:44:55,426 --> 00:44:59,039
Your Honor, in view
of these developments,

875
00:44:59,063 --> 00:45:01,726
the prosecution
moves to dismiss.

876
00:45:12,176 --> 00:45:14,922
I can't believe it,
man... You got me off.

877
00:45:14,946 --> 00:45:17,591
Innocent people are
supposed to get off.

878
00:45:17,615 --> 00:45:19,743
Cliff?

879
00:45:22,353 --> 00:45:24,652
Congratulations.

880
00:45:25,690 --> 00:45:26,900
Thanks.

881
00:45:26,924 --> 00:45:30,070
Ben, thank you.

882
00:45:30,094 --> 00:45:33,073
I don't know how I
ever can repay you.

883
00:45:33,097 --> 00:45:37,644
Well, why don't you and Cliff
go somewhere and talk it over?

884
00:45:37,668 --> 00:45:42,516
Something... new and
good might come of it.

885
00:45:42,540 --> 00:45:44,851
Anywhere you want to go.

886
00:45:44,875 --> 00:45:47,037
Maybe we could talk.

887
00:45:49,113 --> 00:45:51,878
Sure, okay.

888
00:45:53,818 --> 00:45:55,810
Thanks, dude.

889
00:46:00,157 --> 00:46:02,035
Hey, where's he going, man?

890
00:46:02,059 --> 00:46:03,837
We gotta celebrate.

891
00:46:03,861 --> 00:46:06,673
Uh, he's gonna celebrate.

892
00:46:06,697 --> 00:46:10,010
What do you say, Matlock?

893
00:46:10,034 --> 00:46:12,026
Need a lift?

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
